---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Cookie Policy";
const description =
  "Cookie Policy for HowToWriteYourMemoir.com.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article>
    <p><a href="/">← Back to home</a></p>

    <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>

    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> August 1, 2026</p>

    <h2>1. What Are Cookies?</h2>

    <p>
      Cookies are small data files stored on a device when a website is visited.
      Similar technologies may include local storage, pixels, tags, and device
      identifiers.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Current Use of Cookies</h2>

    <p>
      HowToWriteYourMemoir.com aims to use as few cookies and similar
      technologies as reasonably possible.
    </p>

    <p>
      Essential technical or security technologies may be used where necessary
      to deliver, secure, or operate the website.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Analytics Cookies</h2>

    <p>
      Google Analytics 4 and Google Tag Manager must not be activated for
      visitors who require prior consent unless an appropriate consent mechanism
      has been implemented.
    </p>

    <p>
      If analytics is introduced, visitors will be informed of the technologies
      used, their purposes, providers, durations, and available consent choices.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Third-Party Websites</h2>

    <p>
      Links may lead to external websites, including Amazon. Those websites may
      place their own cookies after you visit them.
    </p>

    <p>
      Their cookie practices are governed by their own policies and controls.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Managing Cookies</h2>

    <p>
      You can manage or delete cookies through your browser settings.
    </p>

    <p>
      Blocking essential technologies may affect the operation or security of
      some websites.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Future Consent Controls</h2>

    <p>
      Before non-essential analytics or marketing technologies are activated,
      the website will introduce an appropriate consent control where required.
    </p>

    <p>
      Consent choices should be as easy to withdraw as they are to give.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>

    <p>
      This Cookie Policy may be updated when the website's technologies or
      practices change.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Contact</h2>

    <p>
      Questions about cookies or privacy may be sent to:
      <a href="mailto:[privacy email]">[privacy email]</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
